#
# --- watch matview retains an outdent INTERMEDIATE row (sweeps 1+2, 2026-07-25) ---------
# Verbatim minimized transition list from a keystone sweep. INTERMITTENTLY RED on
# inv-matview-consistent-with-recompute (13 rows vs 12 on recompute). It is a RATE, not a pin —
# a single green run of this suite is weak evidence. Red-for-the-right-reason lock on the open
# IVM watch-matview retract-miss (a row retained at the OLD parent after Outdent re-parents).
#
# 2026-07-26 initial_state probe, 9 isolated runs per arm (HOLON_HAND_AUTHORED_CASE +
# HOLON_HAND_AUTHORED_SIDECAR), run TWICE by independent measurers: 0/9 vs 2/9, then 1/9 vs 1/9
# (unpinned full_headless vs initial_state pinned to storage={Turso} sync={} actors={}). NO wiring
# effect is demonstrated at that sample size (one-sided Fisher exact p = 0.235 for the more
# favourable pair). Both arms reproduce the same signature (watch_view_… matview 13 / recompute 12,
# `bulk-3-5 @ parent bulk-3-0` retained), so the red is the timing race, not the draw.
# The pin is left OFF because it is not shown to help — NOT because it keeps the gate green: this
# case is ~1-in-9 flaky in `just hand-authored` either way (pre-existing, tracked as the open
# inv-matview-consistent-with-recompute red).
# Transition 8 was re-targeted from `block::split-11` to `block:c1` when the position-0 split
