#
# --- page-id rename collision (interim policy, 2026-07-26) -----------------------
# The deterministic witness for the page-identity defect the keystone could not previously
# REACH. Page ids are blake3(path) (`PageId::for_path`), so a collision is only reachable
# temporally: a path must be freed (a rename) and then re-minted (a lazy page-create).
# `RenamePage` + `CreatePageAtFreedPath` close that generator gap.
#
# Sequence: a `pagea` block with one child is converted to a page under the seed page
# `structural-page` (id = H("structural-page/pagea") = block:a6bbdb1d-...); that page is
# renamed to `Renamed` — the id correctly does NOT re-mint, so the path is now free while
# its hash stays occupied; then the freed path is re-created through the production lazy
# page-create op.
#
# INTERIM identity policy (plan §5, RULED 2026-07-26): re-creating a page at a FREED path
# whose derived id is still held by the renamed page is REFUSED FAIL-LOUD — production's
# `create` returns `IdentityCollision` instead of letting `ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE`
# clobber the renamed page. So the RULED interim end-state of this replay is:
#   * transition 6 (CreatePageAtFreedPath) errors visibly; the SUT driver tolerates the
#     `IdentityCollision` and applies NOTHING (the reference models the refusal identically);
#   * NOTHING is clobbered — exactly ONE page survives, titled `Renamed`, with its child;
#   * `inv-every-page-has-its-own-file` stays GREEN because the page rename now removes the
#     old `structural-page/pagea.org` (the D3 double-home fix), so no softening is needed.
# END-STATE (plan §5): a recreate at a freed path will instead mint a unique id and bind the
# NAME to it (two distinct pages); when that lands, flip transition 6's expectation to a
# second page and single-source the mint rule oracle-side.
{"name": "page-id-rename-collision", "description": "Interim identity policy (plan \u00a75): rename A->B then re-create A is REFUSED fail-loud (IdentityCollision) instead of the ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE clobbering the renamed page. Exactly one page survives, titled Renamed; nothing is clobbered. The D3 fix removes the old org file so the page is not double-homed. End-state = unique-mint + name binding.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": []}}, "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "pagea", "id": "block:pgorigin"}}, {"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "child", "id": "block:pgchild"}}, {"Indent": {"block_id": "block:pgchild"}}, {"BlockToPage": {"origin_id": "block:pgorigin"}}, {"RenamePage": {"page_id": "block:a6bbdb1d-4e3d-e3d3-2c8d-c38a0efb5458", "new_title": "Renamed"}}, {"CreatePageAtFreedPath": {"path": "structural-page/pagea"}}]}
#
# --- D2 CLOSED: renaming an org FILE re-homes the doc atomically (Rename port, 2026-07-27) ---
# A user renames `A.org` -> `B.org`. Per the file-move spec a page's title FOLLOWS its
# file name. The FileChange port now carries an ATOMIC `Rename { from }` kind
# (change_source.rs); the in-memory fs's `rename` emits it, the org sync loop routes it to
# `FileSyncController::on_file_renamed`, which re-homes the doc in ONE step: migrate the
# per-file tracking state old->new, re-point the alias, RETITLE the doc-root page to the
# new file stem, and reconcile the moved bytes -- with NO delete-then-create window. So the
# two former entanglements are gone:
#   1. No Remove(A) half fires, so `on_file_deleted`'s cascade-over-delete (the D3 guard
#      cannot close it when the title has not yet followed) never triggers.
#   2. The old file does not linger, so the doc is not double-homed -- inv-every-page-has-
#      its-own-file and inv-blocks-match-ref/org stay GREEN with NO softening.
# The reference (`RefDocumentsMut::rename_document`) and the SUT
# (`SutAppLifecycle::rename_document` -> `FileSystem::rename`) now share the atomic path,
# so the retitle (inv-displayed-text/viewmodel, inv-block-content/block_raw) converges.
# The generator arm stays env-gated OFF (HOLON_PBT_DOC_RENAME) so the RANDOM composed
# alphabet is unchanged; this DETERMINISTIC replay is the un-parked witness (gated by
# `preconditions` alone). Enable the random rung with HOLON_PBT_DOC_RENAME=1.
{"name": "doc-file-rename-title-followed", "description": "D2 CLOSED by the atomic Rename port: a user mv of doc_seed.org -> moved_a.org is delivered as ONE FileChangeKind::Rename{from}, routed to FileSyncController::on_file_renamed. The doc keeps its #+ID (no re-mint), is re-homed to moved_a.org with NO delete-then-create window (so on_file_deleted never cascade-over-deletes it), and its page is retitled to the new file stem moved_a. No old file lingers, so the doc is not double-homed. All invariants un-softened.", "transitions": [{"WriteOrgFile": {"filename": "doc_seed.org", "blocks": [], "keyword_set": null}}, {"RenameDocument": {"old_file_name": "doc_seed.org", "new_file_name": "moved_a.org"}}]}
