# {"name": "pinblock-target-beyond-depth-20-cap-burns-poll-deadline", "description": "QUARANTINED (RED) \u2014 known-reds entry 14, root-caused 2026-08-04. A 24-deep chain: the compiled main-panel matview truncates its recursion at nesting depth 20 (`WHERE _vl2.depth < 20 ... AND _vl2.depth <= 20`, see crates/holon/tests/turso_storage_repros/tabs_main_panel_delivery.rs:130), so dep-0..dep-19 render and dep-20.. do not. `main_editable_descendants()` applies NO depth filter and still offers dep-23, so the generator picks a bullet no user could shift-click. `click_entity_with_modifiers` (user_driver.rs:719) then spins its full 2s poll deadline -- 41 redundant re-snapshots of two watch_view SELECTs -- dispatches NO pin, and reds three invariants from that ONE cause: PINNED PinBlock.sql_reads (91 vs 17), inv-focus-roots (right_sidebar pin missing) and inv-main-panel-rows-match-focus (dep-20..23 truncated). The discriminator is DEPTH, not size: at this same 24-block state target dep-5 costs 17 reads / 272ms vs dep-23 at 91 reads / 2200ms; depth 21 -> 89 and depth 22 -> 101; and a 40-block FLAT panel renders all 40 rows and pins the 40th for 17 reads. Un-comment once the candidate set honours the same depth cap the panel query applies. NOTE this state also independently trips inv-main-panel-rows-match-focus, which must be settled too.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": []}}, "transitions": [{"CreateDocument": {"file_name": "doc_0.org"}}, {"BulkExternalAdd": {"doc_uri": "block:ref-doc-0", "blocks": [{"id": "block:dep-0", "parent_id": "block:ref-doc-0", "content": "depth block 0", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 1785280251381, "updated_at": 1785280251381}, {"id": "block:dep-1", "parent_id": "block:dep-0", "content": "depth block 1", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties":