#
# --- a template instance inherits the definition child's marks (task #23-successor) ---------
# ONE InstantiateTemplate is the whole reproduction. `DirectUserDriver::instantiate_template`
# seeds the definition child `see {{date}} now` with `see` BOLD and `{{date}} now` ITALIC (the
# shared fixture crates/holon-integration-tests/src/template_fixture.rs), and prod's `plan_instantiation`
# carries that mark onto the instance (`remap_marks`, unit-tested in
# crates/holon-api/src/template_instantiation.rs). The reference minted the instance child via
# `Block::new_text` — marks None — so inv-blocks-match-ref/{org,block_raw,matview} reported
# `marks: sut=Some([MarkSpan { start: 0, end: 3, mark: Bold }]) ref=None`. ORACLE gap, not a prod
# bug: the SUT is right. Red log: lane-logs/probe1.log (worktree agent-a53e6a7328cf365e6);
# originally surfaced by the 64-case composed run at
# .claude/worktrees/agent-aa73d6025c345f27f/lane-logs/keystone-green-64.log:1817 once the
# outdent abort (d1642fc2) stopped masking it.
{"name": "template-instance-inherits-definition-marks", "description": "A single InstantiateTemplate on the Turso-only draw: the instance child must carry the definition child's marks, remapped across {{date}} substitution. Bold 0..3 precedes the slot (identity); Italic 4..16 spans the slot AND the text after it, so it must stretch over the substituted value and shift its end (date=krtvhl, 6 scalars for an 8-scalar slot => Italic 4..14). RED before the oracle fix with marks sut=Some([Bold 0..3]) ref=None on the instance child; RED again with a hardcoded ref expectation once the crossing span was added (sut=Some([Bold 0..3, Italic 4..14]) ref=Some([Bold 0..3]), lane-logs/t8-a-red-crossing-mark.txt); GREEN once the reference COMPUTES the remap (template_fixture::instantiate).", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer"]}}, "transitions": [{"InstantiateTemplate": {"parent_id": "block:c1", "date": "krtvhl", "mood": "abcdef"}}]}
