{"name": "padded-raw-link-literal-renders-without-a-degraded-error", "description": "One bulk-created block whose content is the RAW link literal \"[[wJZ9  ]]\" with marks null -- the state every non-org write path (bulk add, MCP, editor cell) stores when a user types a link with a stray space. RED on inv-no-observed-errors with `[ERROR] holon_org_format::models:1289 org render is DEGRADED ... rung=\"Unrepresentable\"`: adoption trims the target (strip_link, inline_marks.rs:572), so the emitted raw bytes re-render as [[wJZ9]] and the ladder's immediate-fixed-point test read that one-step normalization as `NO emission of this block settles`. GREEN once render_candidates emits the ADOPTED form, which costs only the padding adoption was already taking and settles on the first cycle. Whitespace is the only discriminator -- [[wJZ9]] was Exact all along.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer"]}}, "transitions": [{"CreateDocument": {"file_name": "doc_0.org"}}, {"BulkExternalAdd": {"doc_uri": "block:ref-doc-0", "blocks": [{"id": "block:bulk-3-0", "parent_id": "block:ref-doc-0", "content": "r imkbCh", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 1786161835974, "updated_at": 1786161835974}, {"id": "block:bulk-3-4", "parent_id": "block:bulk-3-0", "content": "[[wJZ9  ]]", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 1786161835975, "updated_at": 1786161835975}]}}, {"NavigateFocus": {"region": "main", "block_id": "block:ref-doc-0"}}]}
#
# --- splitting a marked block keeps BOTH halves rich under the Loro CRUD authority (task #8) --
# Nothing covered the marks half of `BlockOperations::split_block` (crates/holon-core/src/traits.rs):
# the new right-half block is created with `BlockContent::RichText { text, marks }` when marks fell
# right of the cursor, and under the Loro-wired draw that create runs through the cell registry
# (Peritext). The marked block is the template instance from the row above (`see krtvhl now`,
# Bold 0..3 + Italic 4..14 — the only mark-carrying block the keystone can mint through production
# ops); splitting at 6 straddles the Italic span. Default (omitted) wiring = full_headless =
# `Wiring::full()`, so Loro is the CRDT authority.
# Mutation-proved (prod is already fixed): withholding the RichText arm reds THIS row at
# transition 2/2 on the right half (marks sut=None ref=Some([Italic 0..8])) while the
# template row above stays GREEN — see lane-logs/t8-b-mutation-red-full.txt and
# lane-logs/t8-b-mutation-isolation.txt.
# NOTE (task #8, measured): the split's OTHER create route — the `!wrote_create_via_cell`
# fallback — IS reached by the composed keystone, but only in SqlOnly-wired draws (8/8 reaches
# on `SqlBlockOperations`, whose create honours the marks param, and always with right_marks==0),
# never on `LoroBlockOperations`. A Loro-only draw carries neither `SutBlockTreeWrite` nor
# `SutTemplateInstantiate`, so no draw both mints a marked block and splits it there.
{"name": "split-of-a-marked-block-keeps-the-right-half-rich-under-loro", "description": "Instantiate the canned template under block:c1, then split its rich instance child (`see krtvhl now`, Bold 0..3 + Italic 4..14) at position 6 under the full_headless (Loro+Turso) wiring. `split_content_marks` partitions the spans and the right half's marks must reach the CRDT authority with the new block's create. Both halves must match the reference: left `see kr` keeps Bold 0..3 and the truncated Italic, right `tvhl now` carries Italic 0..8. RED when split_block's create withholds the RichText marks: right half marks sut=None ref=Some([Italic 0..8]).", "transitions": [{"InstantiateTemplate": {"parent_id": "block:c1", "date": "krtvhl", "mood": "abcdef"}}, {"SplitBlock": {"block_id": "block:0a50d900-c497-53b3-aba8-ef3018423f34", "position": 6}}]}
#
# --- a wiki link AUTHORED IN THE UI is adopted at the write boundary (dogfood 2026-08-08 P1-2) ---
# The creation slot commits the whole typed line through `block.create`, and that is the path
# the dogfood caught: the block was BORN carrying `[[...]]` verbatim with `marks = NULL` and no
# junction row, and only the NEXT boot's file re-ingest adopted it, rewriting the user's stored
# characters with no action of theirs.
# The set_field twin (keystrokes into an already-created block) is deliberately NOT a row here:
# it is covered by `crates/holon/tests/live_edit_link_marks.rs`, and as a keystone row it trips
# two model gaps unrelated to this fix — the reference's editor BUFFER keeps raw markup where the
# SUT's `MutableText` holds the adopted label (the 2026-07-31 ORACLE row, still open), and the
# per-keystroke `TypeChars` SQL budget does not scale with the typed length. Both are named in
# the lane report.
# The target is DANGLING on purpose (no such page exists in the seeded vault): a link whose
# target page EXISTS is additionally rewritten to the resolved `[[block:<id>][Label]]` form by
# the writeback, and the reference does not model link RESOLUTION — that oracle gap is named in
# the lane report, and pinning it here would assert a divergence that is not this fix's subject.
# RED before the fix (lane-logs/t12-keystone-RED.log): the reference did not run the org lens on
# CreateBlockUnderFocus content, so `inv-blocks-match-ref/org` read
#   block:wl0: content: sut="see Wiki Target Page now" ref="see [[Wiki Target Page]] now";
#              marks: sut=Some([Link{Name{"Wiki Target Page"}}]) ref=None
# — the model gap that made every link case inexpressible as a hand-authored row (BugFunnel
# 2026-07-31 ORACLE row). The oracle is fixed FIRST (model states the spec: UI-authored text and
# ingest converge on ONE representation), then the create boundary is fixed to reach it without
# a file round-trip.
{"name": "wiki-link-created-in-the-ui-is-adopted-at-the-write-boundary", "description": "dogfood 2026-08-08 P1-2: a block born from the creation slot with a typed `[[Wiki Target Page]]` must store the STRIPPED label plus a Link mark, like ingest — not raw markup with NULL marks that the next boot silently rewrites.", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "see [[Wiki Target Page]] now", "id": "block:wl0"}}]}
#
# --- a wiki link typed to a page that EXISTS reaches an org fixed point (task #21, re-ruled #32) ---
# The twin of the row above with a RESOLVING target: `Journals` is a seeded page, so the link
# resolves in `block_links` while the stores keep the authored `Name` target.
# Task #21 read that as "the resolved form is the disk truth" and taught BOTH disk-view organs
# the upgrade (SutOrgRender applied `resolve_link_marks`, the ref applied a resolved-link lens),
# which turned the case green over these bytes:
#   inv-org-render-fixed-point (RED, lane-logs/t21-probe-RED-1.log): "render != disk PERSISTED
#     for 5s ... a real echo-loop / oscillation", disk `* see [[block:journals][Journals]] now`
#     vs rendered-from-SQL `* see [[Journals]] now`.
#   inv-blocks-match-ref/org (RED, same log): block:wl1 marks sut=Some([Link{Scheme
#     "block:journals"}]) ref=Some([Link{Name "Journals"}]).
# Martin's ruling (B), 2026-08-08 (task #32), moved the fixed point instead of the oracles:
# write-back emits the AUTHORED bytes, so disk, stores and reference all hold `[[Journals]]`
# and the #21 harness additions are reverted. THE ROW STAYS, ITS MEANING FLIPS -- it now pins
# that the authored form is what settles. Same transitions, same invariants; only the byte the
# fixed point converges on changed, which is exactly what a regression row should notice.
{"name": "wiki-link-to-an-existing-page-reaches-an-org-fixed-point", "description": "task #21, re-ruled by #32 (B): a wiki link typed to a page that EXISTS must reach an org render/disk fixed point on the AUTHORED bytes -- `[[Journals]]` on disk, `Name` marks in every store, resolution only in the block_links junction. Nothing may substitute the resolved id at write-back.", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "see [[Journals]] now", "id": "block:wl1"}}]}
#
# --- birth-then-chord loses the caret (task #58; keystone-smoke red ~1 run in 3) ---------------
# The reference's chord-click model and the SUT's driver must decide "no click happened" from the
# SAME state. The SUT skips its click-time caret seed when `engine.focused_block() == entity`
# (user_driver.rs `click_entity_with_modifiers` / `send_key_chord`); the ref used to skip only
# when the block was its ACTIVE EDITOR. #36's creation-slot birth seats focus AND a caret seed at
# 0 without mounting a ref editor -- a focus-without-editor state that had never existed -- so a
# chord op on the newborn re-seeded the ref caret to end-of-text while the SUT's Tab adopted the
# armed 0. TWO transitions are the whole bug: the `id: null` arm drives the birth gesture, the
# Indent is the first chord op on the newborn. RED at main 4d8b58b7 with `inv-editor-caret/mirror
# ... reference model cursor_byte=1, SUT tracked caret=0`; GREEN once the two predicates are one.
# The random keystone finds this only ~1 run in 3, which is why it is pinned here.
{"name": "birth-then-chord-loses-the-caret", "description": "task #58: after the creation-slot birth gesture (id:null) seats focus in the newborn WITHOUT opening a reference editor, the first chord op on that newborn must NOT re-seed the reference caret to end-of-text -- the SUT's click is skipped (already focused) and its caret stays at the birth-armed 0. Pins model_chord_click_focus against the user_driver.rs skip predicate it mirrors.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Loro", "Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer", "ActionEngine"]}}, "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "a", "id": null}}, {"Indent": {"block_id": "block::create-0"}}]}
#
# --- Enter on the block a caret-0 split just created, in the SHIPPED SqlOnly default ----------
# Keystone-found (2026-08-09 SqlOnly typing-coverage lane), NOVEL. Position-0 semantics are fixed
# by `BlockOperations::split_block` and mirrored by `ReferenceState::split_block`: the id follows
# the TEXT, so the ORIGINAL block keeps the whole text and the newly minted EMPTY block is inserted
# directly ABOVE it. `split_block`'s focus response seats the caret at offset 0 of the text-bearing
# block -- the original -- so the next Enter repeats the shape in place, stacking a second empty
# block above the same id.
# The chord (not a second `SplitBlock` op) is load-bearing: the op alone is GREEN here -- the
# defect needs the editor buffer the keystroke path opens on the block the caret landed in.
# Pinned to storage={Turso} (no Loro) because it is the cell-free editor sink that breaks.
