#
# --- DeleteBackward at caret 0 is a block MERGE, not a keystroke ----------------------------
# The 2026-08-11 keystone minimal counterexample, verbatim. `SplitBlock{position:2}` leaves the
# editor on the NEW tail with the caret at 0, so `DeleteBackward{count:1}` does NOT delete a
# character -- it joins the tail back into its predecessor (block count drops by one, writes=5).
# The `inv-sql-budget` expectation for DeleteBackward was a STATE-BLIND constant modelling only
# the in-buffer backspace (reads REACTIVE_BASE=5, writes 0), so the merge red-lined it:
#   `DeleteBackward.sql_reads: 22 dedup (raw 28, 6 redundant) exceeds 5 + tol 5 = 10`.
# Deterministic: byte-identical assertion 4/4 runs across three revisions (70880807, cdcf59bf,
# 91d3d0f6), independent of the drawn wiring -- an ORACLE defect, never a regression.
# GREEN means the budget reads its state and charges the merge branch a Delete + an Update.
# The 6 redundant re-executions inside the merge are REAL and stay visible in the raw count
# (task #15 redundant-read roster); only the dedup count is under the ceiling.
{"name": "delete-backward-merges-previous-block-budget", "description": "ORACLE red-first pin (2026-08-11 triage): DeleteBackward with the caret at offset 0 merges the block into its previous sibling, which legitimately writes -- the state-blind keystroke budget (reads 5, writes 0) cannot describe it. Wiring pinned to the counterexample's drawn manifest storage={Turso} sync={} actors={}.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": []}}, "transitions": [{"SplitBlock": {"block_id": "block:parent", "position": 2}}, {"DeleteBackward": {"count": 1}}]}

# --- Backspace-at-0 merges into the VISIBLE-OUTLINE predecessor, not the prev sibling --------
# Dogfood 2026-08-18 (Martin, GPUI): with blocks alpha / alpha>beta / alpha>gamma / delta,
# Backspace at the start of `delta` must merge it into `gamma` -- the row directly ABOVE it on
# screen -- and seat the caret there. Prod merged into `alpha`, the previous SIBLING, jumping
# two visible rows up. The reference model encoded the same prev-sibling rule, so the
# differential oracle was blind: model and SUT agreed on the wrong answer. Fixing the model
# first (`join_merge_target`) turns this RED on `inv-blocks-match-ref` (ref: gamma =
# "gammadelta"; SUT: alpha = "alphadelta"), which is the red-for-the-right-reason.
{"name": "join-merges-into-visible-outline-predecessor", "description": "Dogfood 2026-08-18 lock: Backspace at offset 0 in `delta` (last top-level block) merges into `gamma`, the deepest last visible descendant of the previous sibling `alpha` -- NOT into `alpha` itself. Caret lands at gamma's join boundary.", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "alpha", "id": "block:bs-alpha"}}, {"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "beta", "id": "block:bs-beta"}}, {"Indent": {"block_id": "block:bs-beta"}}, {"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "gamma", "id": "block:bs-gamma"}}, {"Indent": {"block_id": "block:bs-gamma"}}, {"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "delta", "id": "block:bs-delta"}}, {"FocusEditableText": {"block_id": "block:bs-delta"}}, {"JoinBlock": {"block_id": "block:bs-delta"}}]}

# --- Backspace at offset 0 in a document's FIRST block is a NO-OP (ruling BS-1(a), 2026-08-18) ---
# `block:parent` is the first child of the seed page `block:structural-page`. With no previous
# sibling, `join_block`'s into_parent arm merged the block into that PAGE — the page's content IS
# its title, so a routine keystroke silently rewrote the document's identity and deleted the block.
# Martin ruled (a): no-op when the parent is a page; into_parent stays for non-page parents.
# Model fixed first (`join_merge_target` returns None for a page parent), so this goes RED on the
# unfixed SUT: ref keeps `parent` and the page title, SUT shows the title with "parent" appended
# and the block gone (inv-blocks-match-ref, inv-block-content).
{"name": "backspace-at-document-start-is-a-noop", "description": "Ruling BS-1(a) lock: Backspace at offset 0 in the FIRST block of a page does nothing — the block survives, the page title is untouched. Pins the into_parent arm's page refusal.", "transitions": [{"FocusEditableText": {"block_id": "block:parent"}}, {"MoveCursor": {"byte_position": 0}}, {"DeleteBackward": {"count": 1}}]}

